WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.429 --> 00:00:04.870
Disney has been churning out family favorite
films for the better part of a century now,

00:00:04.870 --> 00:00:09.600
so there are a ton of great animated and live-action
films to choose from in their collection.

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:13.400
It's becoming increasingly difficult to pin
down which of their movies stand out as the

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:19.070
most important of all, but here are our picks
for the 15 best Disney movies, not including

00:00:19.070 --> 00:00:23.660
those blockbuster Marvel and Star Wars adventures,
of course.

00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:24.660
Up

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:28.740
What makes this movie such an instant classic
is the charming partnership between its main

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:33.380
characters: a young Boy Scout, and a stodgy
old man who retrofits his house to float up,

00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:37.570
up, and away to fulfill his long-denied dream
of getting away from it all with his late

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:38.570
wife.

00:00:38.570 --> 00:00:43.329
Warm and filled with colorful imagery and
one gut-punch of an emotional payoff, Up stands

00:00:43.329 --> 00:00:47.700
out as an unforgettable animated adventure,
and you'll never see helium balloons or golden

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:49.510
retrievers quite the same way.

00:00:49.510 --> 00:00:50.820
"My name is Dug.

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:54.980
I have just met you and I love you."

00:00:54.980 --> 00:00:55.980
Wall-E

00:00:55.980 --> 00:01:00.370
The central characters in Wall-E may not say
much, but the movie remains a showcase of

00:01:00.370 --> 00:01:04.750
what can happen when top-notch animation meets
unbridled creativity.

00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:05.960
"Tada!"

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:09.840
Part dystopian disaster and part love story,
the film offers a devastating look at the

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:14.410
future of mankind and Earth, if our wasteful
ways continue unchecked.

00:01:14.410 --> 00:01:17.970
Wall-E's cute robots only want to make the
world a better place, though, so audiences

00:01:17.970 --> 00:01:23.350
are invited to remain optimistic about the
future without them verbally telling us why.

00:01:23.350 --> 00:01:24.729
Beauty and the Beast

00:01:24.729 --> 00:01:29.060
The story of Belle, Disney's most academically
inclined princess, Beauty and the Beast has

00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:33.360
claimed the hearts of millions for good reason:
at its core, it's about a girl who decides

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:36.869
not to judge a book by its cover and finds
her own happy ending.

00:01:36.869 --> 00:01:41.030
Sure, it's less than ideal that she was imprisoned
by the Beast before falling in love with him.

00:01:41.030 --> 00:01:45.340
But the beauty of this animated classic's
visual dynamism overcomes those flaws to make

00:01:45.340 --> 00:01:50.340
this movie a complete triumph, and the recent
live-action adaptation was almost as compelling

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:52.260
as the original.

00:01:52.260 --> 00:01:53.260
Frozen

00:01:53.260 --> 00:01:58.920
A celebration of both songs and princesses,
Frozen offers not one but two imitable young

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:03.960
ladies, Princesses Anna and Elsa, to fill
the must-have costume racks while transforming

00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:09.170
Hans Christian Andersen's The Snow Queen into
something far less dreary and much more whimsical.

00:02:09.170 --> 00:02:13.420
It's also stunningly beautiful, with an icy
landscape serving as an elegant background

00:02:13.420 --> 00:02:15.920
to the thawing sisterly relationship.

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:19.420
Parents might be more than ready to let the
film's soundtrack go already, but its earworm

00:02:19.420 --> 00:02:23.879
quality is just a small part of what makes
this a must-watch for kids.

00:02:23.879 --> 00:02:24.879
The Incredibles

00:02:24.879 --> 00:02:30.699
This action-adventure flick might've preceded
Marvel's decade of big screen superhero domination,

00:02:30.699 --> 00:02:35.059
but it still holds up as a delightful reminder
of what makes costumed adventure stories so

00:02:35.059 --> 00:02:36.849
fun to watch in the first place.

00:02:36.849 --> 00:02:41.790
Of course, The Incredibles is far more cartoonish
than anything in the MCU, but it takes full

00:02:41.790 --> 00:02:45.999
advantage of the quirky possibilities of an
animated superhero movie with characters that

00:02:45.999 --> 00:02:50.749
boast a broad range of abilities, and it takes
viewers on a heartfelt family journey along

00:02:50.749 --> 00:02:52.760
the way.

00:02:52.760 --> 00:02:54.230
Cinderella

00:02:54.230 --> 00:02:57.849
Cinderella has become a cornerstone of the
Disney catalog, since it's her castle that

00:02:57.849 --> 00:02:59.829
makes up Disney's logo and all.

00:02:59.829 --> 00:03:04.049
Modern audiences might take issue with the
notion that Cinderella only becomes the object

00:03:04.049 --> 00:03:07.879
of her prince's affection after getting a
magical makeover, but Cinderella's staying

00:03:07.879 --> 00:03:13.589
power is as undeniable as her determination
to escape the clutches of her mean stepmonsters.

00:03:13.589 --> 00:03:14.719
Inside Out

00:03:14.719 --> 00:03:19.059
This Disney-Pixar adventure takes a clever
look of the way the human mind works, animating

00:03:19.059 --> 00:03:23.480
the emotions and impulses fighting for control
of its main character while trying to protect

00:03:23.480 --> 00:03:26.049
the core memories making up the basis of her
personality.

00:03:26.049 --> 00:03:27.049
"No dessert?

00:03:27.049 --> 00:03:28.049
Oh sure.

00:03:28.049 --> 00:03:30.579
We'll eat our dinner right after you eat this,
AGHHHH!"

00:03:32.960 --> 00:03:37.700
In the story, our young heroine Riley has
to adjust to a new life as her family relocates

00:03:37.700 --> 00:03:41.909
to another city, and that shift is the spark
that sends her from the happy-go-lucky child

00:03:41.909 --> 00:03:46.439
she once was into the rebellious tween phase
— a change that happens to most people at

00:03:46.439 --> 00:03:51.249
some point anyway, so it feels very familiar
and authentically adolescent.

00:03:51.249 --> 00:03:55.790
Rather than rely upon constructs of fiction,
like most cartoons, Inside Out borrows from

00:03:55.790 --> 00:04:00.389
reality to offer some heavy truths in an amusing
animated package.

00:04:00.389 --> 00:04:01.989
Mary Poppins

00:04:01.989 --> 00:04:02.989
Author P.L.

00:04:02.989 --> 00:04:07.249
Travers was infamously unhappy with Disney's
adaptation of her story, but Mary Poppins

00:04:07.249 --> 00:04:10.389
arrived in theaters as an instant musical
evergreen.

00:04:10.389 --> 00:04:14.049
We can thank the movie's depiction of its
eponymous magical nanny for memorable songs

00:04:14.049 --> 00:04:18.820
like "A Spoonful of Sugar" and for raising
the musical and visual bar on the genre as

00:04:18.820 --> 00:04:20.430
a whole.

00:04:20.430 --> 00:04:21.870
Aladdin

00:04:21.870 --> 00:04:26.300
Disney really did take audiences to a whole
new world with this animated hit.

00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:30.699
Aladdin centered on the rags-to-riches story
of a "street rat" who stumbles upon a magic

00:04:30.699 --> 00:04:34.791
lamp containing a 10,000 year old genie, who
was all too happy to join him on his magic

00:04:34.791 --> 00:04:35.791
carpet ride.

00:04:35.791 --> 00:04:40.840
The stunning scenery, music, and all the other
memorable characters are all beyond reproach.

00:04:40.840 --> 00:04:46.039
But it's Robin Williams' Genie that really
elevates the picture to hilarious new heights.

00:04:46.039 --> 00:04:47.620
Peter Pan

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:51.130
If there's one thing we learned from Peter
Pan, it's to never surrender that sense of

00:04:51.130 --> 00:04:55.000
youth and wonder… and, of course, to never
smile at a crocodile.

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:59.500
There've been many terrible attempts to recreate
the magic of Peter Pan and his Never Never

00:04:59.500 --> 00:05:03.930
Land, but nothing has come close to touching
the simple sophistication of the first version,

00:05:03.930 --> 00:05:07.639
which thrust its sleepy little heroes into
a living dream that played with elements of

00:05:07.639 --> 00:05:11.639
fantasy, like mermaids, fairies, and sniveling
old pirates.

00:05:11.639 --> 00:05:15.690
The film is fun, plain and simple, and mostly
stands the test of time because, like its

00:05:15.690 --> 00:05:17.639
title character, it never gets old.

00:05:17.639 --> 00:05:19.150
Alice in Wonderland

00:05:19.150 --> 00:05:24.310
The animated adaptation of Lewis Carroll's
story is a visual extravaganza that plays

00:05:24.310 --> 00:05:26.430
well to children and adults alike.

00:05:26.430 --> 00:05:30.979
The movie follows its title character down
the rabbit hole into a dreamlike, and, at

00:05:30.979 --> 00:05:35.460
times, nightmarish — land of otherworldly
creatures that challenge her wits and resolve.

00:05:35.460 --> 00:05:39.590
The eerie landscapes were bested only by its
cast of memorable characters.

00:05:39.590 --> 00:05:44.360
The movie is the definition of trippy and
still stands above the studio's live-action

00:05:44.360 --> 00:05:45.719
remake.

00:05:45.719 --> 00:05:47.289
Finding Nemo

00:05:47.289 --> 00:05:51.090
Finding Dory might've been more commercially
successful than its predecessor, but Finding

00:05:51.090 --> 00:05:55.290
Nemo set the tone for its successful sequel
in virtually every way.

00:05:55.290 --> 00:05:59.759
The film followed a clownfish named Marlin
and a forgetful Blue tang named Dory on their

00:05:59.759 --> 00:06:04.999
exhausting adventure to find Marlin's lost
son Nemo within an actual ocean of obstacles.

00:06:04.999 --> 00:06:08.689
While Finding Dory certainly touched on all
of the successful elements of the first film,

00:06:08.689 --> 00:06:11.789
namely, tracking down a missing fish who's
been scooped from the sea with the help of

00:06:11.789 --> 00:06:16.840
some adorable finny friends, the soul of the
first adventure was so much stronger.

00:06:16.840 --> 00:06:18.449
Lady and the Tramp

00:06:18.449 --> 00:06:22.110
Even thinking about the spaghetti scene in
Lady and the Tramp is bound to induce feelings

00:06:22.110 --> 00:06:24.159
of both hunger and romance.

00:06:24.159 --> 00:06:28.659
This story of a proper society pooch who accidentally
lands herself in the company of strays is

00:06:28.659 --> 00:06:34.030
a pure delight, and while Disney's 101 Dalmations
also had a full-on litter of doggies to love,

00:06:34.030 --> 00:06:39.340
there's simply no film furbaby quite as graceful
as Miss Lady Ma'am, whose friends are also

00:06:39.340 --> 00:06:42.719
as human as any two-legged type could hope
to be.

00:06:42.719 --> 00:06:44.539
Toy Story 3

00:06:44.539 --> 00:06:48.129
This may have been the third outing for Woody,
Buzz, and the rest of the gang, but Toy Story

00:06:48.129 --> 00:06:52.310
3 outshone the previous two installments in
the way of emotional impact.

00:06:52.310 --> 00:06:56.189
The film picks up with Andy heading off to
college, where having a cowboy and space doll

00:06:56.189 --> 00:06:58.379
won't earn him any cool points in his dorm.

00:06:58.379 --> 00:07:02.219
The toys are packed up for the attic but are
accidentally sent to a daycare filled with

00:07:02.219 --> 00:07:04.020
reckless children and a bully bear.

00:07:04.020 --> 00:07:08.009
Together, they have to fight their way back
to where they belong… wherever that might

00:07:08.009 --> 00:07:10.080
be now that Andy's no longer a kid.

00:07:10.080 --> 00:07:14.539
Their journey offers an emotional parable
about the process of abandoning childish things

00:07:14.539 --> 00:07:19.129
and really resonates with audiences, particularly
adults who might've been surprised to find

00:07:19.129 --> 00:07:24.370
themselves bawling over the lost toys that
symbolized so many bittersweet bygones.

00:07:24.370 --> 00:07:25.669
The Lion King

00:07:25.669 --> 00:07:30.879
This family favorite really does offer the
full circle of Disney's animated strengths.

00:07:30.879 --> 00:07:35.600
The film is rich with stunning landscapes
and teeming with character variety and morals;

00:07:35.600 --> 00:07:40.029
on top of all that, there are deeply identifiable
sets of emotion at play.

00:07:40.029 --> 00:07:44.249
For kids, it's easy to understand Simba's
joy, desperation for freedom, and his sense

00:07:44.249 --> 00:07:46.490
of being lost without his family framework.

00:07:46.490 --> 00:07:51.679
For parents, protecting your kids at all costs
becomes the most base instinct of all, so

00:07:51.679 --> 00:07:53.849
everything about this movie's story rings
true.

00:07:53.849 --> 00:07:56.469
"Let an old pro show you how it's done."

00:07:56.469 --> 00:08:01.089
Add in one outstanding soundtrack, and it's
no wonder The Lion King still reigns supreme.

